  "_doc": "The CmuxNext targets that build on Linux (plans/cmux-next/chrome-parity/p15-oracle.md section H). Edit waves, new, excludedPackages and ffi; `generated` is written by scripts/cmux-next/linux/linux-tier.py from swift package dump-package, and the same script copies ffi and the generated lists into the Linux mode of Package.swift (CMUX_SWIFTPM_TARGET_LINUX=1 on Linux), which reads no file so that SwiftPM's manifest cache sees every change. Run it after a Package.swift or tier change; --check says when either is stale. A tier target keeps only its dependencies inside the tier: the dropped ones are listed under generated.blockedEdges, and their compile errors are the Linux work queue (swift-tier.sh --errors-queue).",
